From: gt-be98-buildroot <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd 2.12: no_pri_sec_switch is a configuration item (keep
 the configured 5 GHz primary)

hostapd 2.12 has the field (struct hostapd_config no_pri_sec_switch, read by
src/ap/hw_features.c ieee80211n_check_40mhz and ieee80211n_check_40mhz_5g)
but no configuration-file key: nothing in the hostapd tree sets it, and a
"no_pri_sec_switch=1" line fails the whole file ("unknown configuration
item", checked with hostapd's own parser). Without it a fixed 5 GHz
[HT40+] BSS may come up on its SECONDARY 20 MHz channel: check_40mhz_5g
swaps primary and secondary when the pre-start scan hears beacons on the
secondary but not on the primary (gt-be98: configured 36/80 came up on
5200 MHz in 4 of 60 starts, so clients that look for 5180 miss it).

With no_pri_sec_switch=1 ieee80211n_check_40mhz returns before the
pre-start 40 MHz scan: the configured primary is used as is. On 5 GHz that
scan can only swap (check_40mhz_5g never drops the BSS to 20 MHz when it has
scan results), so the swap is all that is lost. The DFS paths do not read the
field: dfs.c picks a block with its first channel as primary (HT40+), a CSA
does not run the scan, and a restart after a radar keeps the picked primary
instead of re-swapping it. Default 0 (unchanged behaviour).

diff -ru a/hostapd/config_file.c b/hostapd/config_file.c
--- a/hostapd/config_file.c
+++ b/hostapd/config_file.c
@@ -3678,6 +3678,8 @@
 		conf->ht_vht_twt_responder = atoi(pos);
 	} else if (os_strcmp(buf, "obss_interval") == 0) {
 		conf->obss_interval = atoi(pos);
+	} else if (os_strcmp(buf, "no_pri_sec_switch") == 0) {
+		conf->no_pri_sec_switch = atoi(pos);
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AC
 	} else if (os_strcmp(buf, "ieee80211ac") == 0) {
 		conf->ieee80211ac = atoi(pos);
diff -ru a/hostapd/hostapd.conf b/hostapd/hostapd.conf
--- a/hostapd/hostapd.conf
+++ b/hostapd/hostapd.conf
@@ -673,6 +673,12 @@
 # no co-existence issues with neighboring devices are found.
 #obss_interval=0
 
+# no_pri_sec_switch: Keep the configured primary channel of a 5 GHz HT40/VHT/HE/EHT
+# BSS. 0 = hostapd may swap the primary and secondary 20 MHz channels after its
+# pre-start 20/40 MHz coexistence scan (default); 1 = no swap and no pre-start
+# 40 MHz scan (ieee80211n_check_40mhz); the configured primary is used as is.
+#no_pri_sec_switch=0
+
 # ht_vht_twt_responder: Whether TWT responder is enabled in HT and VHT modes
 # 0 = disable; Disable TWT responder support in  HT and VHT modes (default).
 # 1 = enable; Enable TWT responder support in HT and VHT modes if supported by
